            "count": 0,
            "bug_id": 19317,
            "text": "eval(), R_forceAndCall() and bcEval_loop() each keep an RCNTXT in their stack frame for the builtin-call context, which is set up only while profiling or (in the first two) for foreign calls such as .Call(). One such frame is held per level whenever R code recurses through C: do.call(), lapply(), eval(), S3 dispatch.\n\nReproducible example: builtin-context-stack-repro.R, attached, prints the depth reached before \"C stack usage is too close to the limit\". With an 8 MB stack on macOS arm64 (r90883, clang) it is 1959 through do.call(), 1936 through lapply() and 1750 through eval(); with the patch 2833, 2770 and 2418.\n\nProposed patch: attached as builtin-context-helper.diff, against r90883. It moves the context, with the begincontext()/endcontext() sequence, into one helper shared by the three callers and kept out of line with R_NOINLINE (the macro from the patch in bug 19315; the Defn.h hunk is identical). The three frames shrink from 592, 528 and 1712 bytes to 160, 112 and 1328; when a context is created is unchanged.\n\nmake check passes, and tracebacks and error calls from foreign calls are as before. The patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/484, where CI results can be seen.",
            "tags": [],
            "is_private": false,
            "id": 104234
          },
          {
