          {
            "id": 104237,
            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Created attachment 4064\npatch: allocate builtin-call contexts on the node stack (applies on top of attachment 4062)\n\nA possible further step, on top of attachment 4062: builtin-context-pool.diff, attached, allocates the builtin context on the byte code node stack, as is done for inlined closure calls, instead of in the helper's frame. That frame shrinks from 512 bytes to 80, and with an 8 MB stack, recursion through a foreign call from interpreted code or forceAndCall(), or through a builtin call while profiling, gets 7 to 12% deeper. There is no speed benefit.\n\nIt is a trade-off, though: each active context takes 448 bytes of node stack, so with a 64 MB C stack the node stack runs out first and the same recursion gets shallower (from 14531 to 6658 levels while profiling; builtin-context-pool-repro.R, attached).\n\nmake check passes. Patch also at https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/485.",
